 {
  "id": "acme-db",
  "conversation_id": "acme-db",
  "title": "Acme Notes: database choice",
  "create_time": 1772618400.0,
  "current_node": "acme-db-5",
  "mapping": {
   "acme-db-root": {
    "id": "acme-db-root",
    "message": null,
    "parent": null,
    "children": [
     "acme-db-0"
    ]
   },
   "acme-db-0": {
    "id": "acme-db-0",
    "parent": "acme-db-root",
    "children": [
     "acme-db-1"
    ],
    "message": {
     "id": "acme-db-0",
     "author": {
      "role": "user"
     },
     "create_time": 1772618400.0,
     "content": {
      "content_type": "text",
      "parts": [
       "I'm starting Acme Notes, a collaborative note-taking app. Postgres or MongoDB for the user store?"
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   "acme-db-1": {
    "id": "acme-db-1",
    "parent": "acme-db-0",
    "children": [
     "acme-db-2"
    ],
    "message": {
     "id": "acme-db-1",
     "author": {
      "role": "assistant"
     },
     "create_time": 1772618490.0,
     "content": {
      "content_type": "text",
      "parts": [
       "Both can work. MongoDB gives schema flexibility; Postgres gives relational integrity, joins and mature tooling. What do your access patterns look like?"
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   "acme-db-2": {
    "id": "acme-db-2",
    "parent": "acme-db-1",
    "children": [
     "acme-db-3"
    ],
    "message": {
     "id": "acme-db-2",
     "author": {
      "role": "user"
     },
     "create_time": 1772618580.0,
     "content": {
      "content_type": "text",
      "parts": [
       "Users belong to orgs, orgs share notebooks, notebooks have permissions per user. Lots of joins."
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   "acme-db-3": {
    "id": "acme-db-3",
    "parent": "acme-db-2",
    "children": [
     "acme-db-4"
    ],
    "message": {
     "id": "acme-db-3",
     "author": {
      "role": "assistant"
     },
     "create_time": 1772618670.0,
     "content": {
      "content_type": "text",
      "parts": [
       "That's strongly relational. Postgres fits well; with MongoDB you'd end up re-implementing joins in application code."
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   "acme-db-4": {
    "id": "acme-db-4",
    "parent": "acme-db-3",
    "children": [
     "acme-db-5"
    ],
    "message": {
     "id": "acme-db-4",
     "author": {
      "role": "user"
     },
     "create_time": 1772618760.0,
     "content": {
      "content_type": "text",
      "parts": [
       "Ok, decided: we go with Postgres, not MongoDB. We need joins across users, orgs and notebooks."
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   "acme-db-5": {
    "id": "acme-db-5",
    "parent": "acme-db-4",
    "children": [],
    "message": {
     "id": "acme-db-5",
     "author": {
      "role": "assistant"
     },
     "create_time": 1772618850.0,
     "content": {
      "content_type": "text",
      "parts": [
       "Great. I'll sketch the schema with users, orgs, memberships and notebooks tables."
      ]
     }
    }
   }
  }
 },
